# Line endings.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out files to CRLF.
# For most files that is harmless. For the two Maven wrapper scripts it is not:
# they are executed as shell scripts, and a CRLF `#!/bin/sh\r` makes the kernel
# look for an interpreter named "sh\r". Inside the Docker build that surfaces as
# `exit code 127` on `./mvnw` with no useful message, which is exactly how
# `docker compose --build` failed on 2026-09-15.
#
# It also explains why `weldforge-auth/mvnw` has shown as permanently modified
# in `git status` for months: the committed file is LF, the working copy is
# CRLF, and nothing ever reconciled them.
#
# `text eol=lf` pins these regardless of the local autocrlf setting.
* text=auto

mvnw            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
gradlew         text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts stay CRLF.
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
mvnw.cmd        text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.svg           text
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.jar           binary
